    "behaviour": {"x": 470, "y": 0, "w": 600, "fill": "blue", "size": "m", "text": "F3 decisions (product owner, 2026-11-16)\n\n1. A blue \"Record a deed\" button sits in the header on every page. The menu is Home · My QR · Profile; Log out moves into Profile.\n2. No invite option (invites are off). The hub shows a guidance line instead: \"Doer not on Good Deeds? Ask them to sign up, then show you their QR.\"\n3. Limits (new rule, backend change pending): at most 15 reports per person you record per month, and 150 in total. Warnings appear only when close: from 3 left for one person (on the deed form), from 10 left in total (on the hub).\n4. Location: explain first, then the phone's permission prompt. Without location nothing can be verified.\n5. Photos: optional, up to 4 per report (a config value), taken with the camera or uploaded, below the description. Faces of people being helped are blurred automatically. Where photos are stored (Azure Blob, S3 or Google Cloud Storage) is decided later.\n\nFlow: Hub → location (first time) → scan or ID + code → checking → deed form (send within 15 min) → verified.\nWhen? is limited to 2 h before the scan. Ahmed can be recognised by the same person once a day.\n\nPress Play on the prototype: Scan → Allow → tap the viewfinder to simulate a scan → add photos → Send."}
